on:** â€”\n48\t\n49\t**done-when:** Verifiable ON DEMAND (run `morning_briefing.py` against the live KB and inspect the\n50\temitted session_note/`latest_summary.json` â€” the 06:47 deadline is a deploy deadline, not the\n51\tacceptance gate): the session_note contains zero raw IDs and zero `local:`/vendor/paper entries;\n52\tevery top find is a named eligible artifact with a why-line; the productivity line reads\n53\t\"suggestion adoption\" with window + sample size; one clean commit; `python -m pytest` green with\n54\tadditive-only test changes.\n55\t\n56\t- **Given** today's real KB (mis-kinded arxiv rows included), **when** the briefing runs, **then** top_finds contains only eligible non-paper/non-model/non-local artifacts with `name/kind/why` fields and the session_note renders them as named lines.\n57\t- **Given** a FIXTURE hh_events set of 20 distinct queries of which 5 have â‰¥1 `loaded`, **when** the index computes, **then** it reports 25% adoption, window=all-time (labeled fallback because the 7-day window has <10 queries), sample_size=20 â€” never a bare 0% from a thin window; a separate live sanity check asserts adoption âˆˆ [0,1] and a labeled window. [SUBTLE â€” the 0%-with-status-ok trap]\n58\t- **Given** an artifact with `local:` canonical_url or a vendor-denylist domain, **then** it can never appear in top_finds (regression-tested).\n59\t- **Given** zero hh_events queries ever (fixture), **then** status is `no_data` (and only then).\n60\t\n61\t## Wave 2 â€” Right kind at ingest + catalog backfills + serving-surface trust\n62\t\n63\t**Intent:** Stop noise at the source and make the existing catalog trustworthy: arxivâ†’paper at\n64\tscreen time, vendor/blog rejection with a registry allowlist, the awesome-list fix at its real root\n65\tcause (the discovery-queue DRAIN path, E21 â€” the scout-level fix already exists), audited backfills\n66\tthat own the library filesystem (dir-moves, E22), the publisher retired_at predicate placed where it\n67\tactually executes (E20), and the D1/D2 Helping Hand scoping â€” BOTH halves of it.\n68\t\n69\t**Deliverables:** `roles/static_screener.py`: arxiv URL/slug â†’ `kind='paper'` at screen time;\n70\tsource-type gate rejecting vendor/blog/aggregator/personal-blog URLs with an explicit ALLOWLIST for\n71\tpackage registries (pypi/npm/crates.io/nuget/maven/gitlab) so legit non-GitHub tools survive\n72\t(Stage-2 audit: crates.io et al. would otherwise be false positives); pointer-description reject as\n73\tdrain backstop; every reject audited as JSONL to `reports/screen_rejects/<date>.jsonl` (reason +\n74\tURL + sweep â€” the `--audit-out` file pattern; decided: a FILE, not a table â€” no migration, and\n75\t0025 stays reserved for Wave 4). Drain-path fix: `FetchedSource` gains a `discovery_queue_origin`\n76\tflag set in `roles/scout.py::_discovery_source` (lines 338-352); orchestrator branch (the\n77\t`fetched.extend(drained)` seam at orchestrator.py:663): a drained source that is itself a link list\n78\t(**â‰¥10 markdown links and zero installable-content markers** â€” no SKILL.md front-matter, no\n79\tmanifest/setup/pyproject) re-enqueues its links via the existing `_DISCOVERED_LINKS` buffer +\n80\t`flush_discovery_buffer` (INSERT OR IGNORE dedupe) instead of being screened.\n81\t`bin/backfill_paper_kind.py`: UPDATE-only re-kind of all arxiv tool/agent rows resolved by rule\n82\t(detection reused from `migrate_to_kind_paper.py:115-125`; ~96 as of 2026-06-09; its DELETE step is\n83\tdead â€” E16); filesystem owned via dir-move `library/{agents,tools}/<slug>/ â†’ library/papers/<slug>/`\n84\t(page-write fallback only where no source dir; curated-card skip-guard preserved) +\n85\t`regenerate_indexes` (heals the 109 pre-existing dead `papers/` links); deletes superseded dirs\n86\tidempotently on EVERY run; `--dry-run` + `--audit-out` + its own log file (E23: the briefing .cmd\n87\ttruncates the shared log); hooked into `run-morning-briefing.cmd` AND `run-agents.cmd` ahead of\n88\ttheir publisher calls. Retire backfills (set `retired_at`, never DELETE; dry-run + audit each;\n89\tworking sets resolved by rule in the audit pass): the developer.nvidia.com tool rows (~50); the\n90\tpointer rows (`short_description LIKE 'Awesome-list reference to%'`, ~31-34); ALL same-arxiv-base-id\n91\tversion pairs, keep-latest, alias old slugs (8 pairs as of 2026-06-09 and growing nightly until this\n92\twave ships). Retire backfills ALSO delete the retired rows' library dirs idempotently + run\n93\t`regenerate_indexes` â€” the same filesystem-ownership pattern as the re-kind dir-moves.\n94\t`publisher.py`: unconditional `retired_at` predicate evaluated BEFORE the `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE`\n95\tearly-return (publisher.py:78-79); snapshot scrubs retired pages; regression tests run with the env\n96\tvar UNSET (extend `tests/test_snapshot_scrub.py`). HH server (per D1/D2): `recent_summary`\n97\t(server.py:1386-1391) filters `retired_at` and stops counting models/papers as finds; **D1:**\n98\t`kind='model'` excluded from single-mode routing + `_record_surfaced` telemetry but kept in\n99\tranked/compare paths (mode branch at server.py:749-772); **D2:** papers REMAIN in the match pool\n100\tfor pull queries with `kind` clearly labeled in match output (regression test: papers are never\n101\texcluded from `_compute_matches`, and a matched paper is never auto-loaded); plugin rebuild\n102\t(`bin/build-plugin.py`) + reinstall (MANUAL â€” John installs in Cowork) + live `recent_summary`\n103\tsmoke. `bin/noise_audit.py`: standing zero-noise check (arxiv-as-tool/agent, vendor tools, pointer\n104\tartifacts, dead library links, retired-in-surfaces) + fixture tests; failure surfaces in the\n105\tnightly summary. Cross-surface count regression tests (briefing counts vs recent_summary vs\n106\tpublisher snapshot) land here.\n107\t\n108\t**Depends on:** Wave 1\n109\t\n110\t**done-when:** `bin/noise_audit.py` returns 0 on the live KB; retired rows absent from the publisher\n111\tsnapshot, recent_summary, and the library; the drain path re-enqueues link lists instead of minting\n112\tartifacts (fixture-tested); papers matchable-and-labeled in HH pull (fixture-tested), models scoped\n113\tper D1; all backfills ran with audits saved; plugin rebuilt + handed to John for reinstall + smoked\n114\tafter reinstall; clean committed tree; `python -m pytest` green.\n115\t\n116\t- **Given** an arxiv URL in any sweep, **when** screened, **then** kind='paper' â€” no path mints an arxiv tool/agent (fixture-tested per sweep).\n117\t- **Given** a crates.io/pypi/npm tool URL, **when** screened, **then** it is NOT rejected by the source gate (allowlist regression test). [SUBTLE â€” the false-positive trap]\n118\t- **Given** a drained discovery_queue item with â‰¥10 markdown links and no installable-content markers, **then** its links are re-enqueued (INSERT OR IGNORE) and no artifact row is created.\n119\t- **Given** `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` unset (production), **when** the snapshot builds, **then** a retired artifact's page is absent. [SUBTLE â€” the dead-code-placement trap, E20]\n120\t- **Given** a pull query matching a paper, **then** it is returned with kind='paper' visibly labeled and is never auto-loaded; **given** a single-mode query, **then** no model row is routed or recorded as surfaced. [D1/D2]\n121\t- **Given** the backfill runs twice, **then** the second run is a no-op (idempotent dir-moves and re-kinds; audit shows zero changes).\n122\t\n123\t## Wave 3 â€” Weekly digest v1 + notability signal\n124\t\n125\t**Intent:** Ship the human-facing digest (papers' only push surface â€” criterion 6) and light up the\n126\talready-built-but-never-scheduled link-health probe so stars/staleness exist as signals.\n127\t\n128\t**PRECONDITION (MANUAL/environmental):** authenticated gh CLI â€” verify `& 'C:\\Program Files\\GitHub\n129\tCLI\\gh.exe' auth status` before the backfill; HALT-AND-ASK John if unauthenticated (unauthenticated\n130\tis 60 req/hr â€” a multi-hour stall; the authenticated path is minutes).\n131\t\n132\t**Deliverables:** `bin/setup-tasks.ps1` registers `bin/check_link_health.py` as a weekly scheduled\n133\ttask (idempotent registration, mirroring the existing 5 tasks); one supervised backfill run over the\n134\tactive GitHub-linked artifacts (283 as of 2026-06-09; probe selection keys on `canonical_url LIKE\n135\t'%github.com%'` since `github_full_name` is never populated). `bin/weekly_digest.py` + weekly\n136\tscheduled task: \"what's genuinely worth knowing this week\" â€” top finds of the week (Wave-1\n137\teligibility gate + stars now available as a quality signal) with why-lines; **papers worth reading**\n138\t(newest/most-notable `kind='paper'` rows â€” the Stage-0 opt-in stream); catalog-health deltas\n139\t(retired/deduped/new this week). Output `reports/weekly/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`; delivered via the existing\n140\t`briefing_delivery` channel (toast + session_note pointer). Unit tests with fixture KB; task\n141\tregistration idempotency test pattern reused.\n142\t\n143\t**Depends on:** Wave 2\n144\t\n145\t**done-when:** â‰¥80% of active GitHub-linked artifacts (measured at run time) have `gh_stargazers`\n146\tpopulated; the weekly task is registered; digest #1 is generated from the real KB and delivered\n147\t(toast + pointer); stars appear in top-find quality signals where present; clean committed tree;\n148\t`python -m pytest` green.\n149\t\n150\t- **Given** the backfill run completes, **then** `link_health` holds probed rows for â‰¥80% of active GitHub-linked artifacts with stargazer counts, and a re-run respects the 7-day idempotency.\n151\t- **Given** a generated digest, **then** it contains only eligible ranked finds with why-lines, a clearly-separated papers section, and health deltas â€” and zero raw IDs.\n152\t- **Given** the digest task fires with an empty week, **then** it degrades gracefully (states \"quiet week\", no crash, no empty-section noise).\n153\t\n154\t## Wave 4 â€” The taste score\n155\t\n156\t**Intent:** Replace the interim heuristic with a persisted interestingness score tuned to John's\n157\tprofile, correctly priced and metered (E17: unpriced tags meter $0 and `default_models` is\n158\truntime-inert â€” the priced key and the called tag must be provably identical). Scope per the master\n159\tcut list: new finds + any unscored artifact reaching a serving surface â€” never the full back catalog.\n160\t\n161\t**Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml`: priced key for the chosen taste model (+ `verification:` block,\n162\t`verified:false` permitted) and a `default_models.taste` entry; `roles/taste.py` resolves its model\n163\tfrom `default_models.taste` with `AURORA_TASTE_MODEL` env override â€” a unit test asserts the\n164\tresolved tag has a non-zero priced rate (extends `tests/test_pricing_keys.py`). Migration\n165\t`kb/migrations/0025_interest_score.sql` (additive; next free number, verified; mirror in\n166\t`kb/schema.sql`): `artifacts.interest_score REAL`, `interest_why TEXT`, `interest_scored_at TEXT`.\n167\t`docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`: versioned, John-editable profile (Claude/agent ecosystem; usable >\n168\tacademic; novelty over volume) â€” seeded in this wave, edited only by John thereafter.\n169\t`roles/taste.py`: scorer for (a) new non-paper, non-retired finds nightly and (b) any unscored\n170\tartifact that becomes a top_finds/digest candidate (so serving surfaces never rank NULL-scored\n171\trows); inputs short_description + incorporation_note + `gh_stargazers` + kind; every call metered\n172\tthrough CostRecorder; nightly call cap (env `AURORA_TASTE_NIGHTLY_CAP`, default 40) with heuristic\n173\tfallback (stars+badge+kind-priority, persisted as the score with NULL `interest_why`) when capped or\n174\ton LLM failure; wired into the orchestrator post-librarian step. Precedence: `interest_why` drives\n175\tranking surfaces; `incorporation_note` stays the library \"how to incorporate\" voice. Ranking switch:\n176\ttop_finds (morning_briefing) + weekly digest order by `interest_score` (any residual NULL sorts\n177\tbelow scored, then the Wave-1 heuristic as tiebreak); why-lines upgrade to `interest_why` when present.\n178\t\n179\t**Depends on:** Wave 3\n180\t\n181\t**done-when:** Checkable ON DEMAND inside the build: a supervised capped run of `roles/taste.py`\n182\tover K existing unscored serving-surface candidates produces `interest_score` + `interest_why` with\n183\tnon-zero metered cost rows (â‰¤ the cap); fixture tests prove cap/fallback/ranking behavior; top finds\n184\t+ digest order by the score; the profile doc exists and is referenced; clean committed tree;\n185\t`python -m pytest` green. **SEPARATELY-VERIFIED (armed, not demonstrated in-build):** the nightly\n186\tleg â€” every new find from subsequent nightly runs arrives scored; verified by John from the next\n187\tmorning's data, mirroring the Wave-5 fixture-based pattern.\n188\t\n189\t- **Given** a taste call, **then** its `costs` row prices against the same tag taste.py resolved (no $0 fiction). [SUBTLE â€” the unpriced-tag trap, E17]\n190\t- **Given** the nightly cap is hit or the LLM fails, **then** remaining finds get the heuristic score persisted + NULL `interest_why` (no crash, no unscored-and-unranked rows).\n191\t- **Given** a scored and an unscored artifact, **then** ranking places scored-by-interest first, falling back to the Wave-1 heuristic â€” never raw recency alone; **given** a top_finds/digest candidate with NULL score, **then** it is scored (LLM or heuristic) before surfacing.\n192\t\n193\t## Wave 5 â€” Close the loop\n194\t\n195\t**Intent:** Usage shifts what surfaces (criterion 4), the catalog self-maintains (criterion 5), and\n196\tthe digest shows John whether Aurora is actually helping.\n197\t\n198\t**Deliverables:** Bounded usage modifier in the HH server `_compute_matches` (server.py:629-683,\n199\tpost-cosine â€” the repetition gate at lines 779-824 is the read-telemetry-at-match-time precedent):\n200\tper-a