ght sweeps, so the\ndeploy deadline is 06:47, not 01:07). No DB or pipeline changes in this wave; the briefing-side\nqueries carry their own noise exclusions so they are correct even though tonight's rows are still\nmis-kinded (E3: `upsert_artifact` never updates kind, so nothing the sweeps do can undo this wave).\n\n**Deliverables:** `morning_briefing.py` top_finds query (currently `id DESC LIMIT 5`, model-only\nexclusion, lines 1075-1082) replaced with: positive eligibility gate (`github_full_name IS NOT NULL\nOR canonical_url LIKE '%github.com%' OR confidence_badge IS NOT NULL` â€” note `github_full_name` is\ncurrently NULL on every row, so the URL branch is the live path) AND `canonical_url NOT LIKE\n'local:%'` (E19: self-finds would headline otherwise); noise exclusions in-query (kind NOT IN\n('model','paper'), arxiv URL/slug patterns reused from `migrate_to_kind_paper.py:115-125`, a\nVENDOR_DENYLIST constant seeded with developer.nvidia.com, pointer-description `LIKE 'Awesome-list\nreference to%'`); rank = confidence_badge presence â†’ kind priority (skill>agent>tool>template) â†’\nrecency; each entry emits ADDITIVE fields `name/kind/why/quality` â€” `why` = first sentence of\nshort_description, U+FFFD stripped (explicitly interim until Wave 4's `interest_why`); `quality`\nemitted only when discriminating (badge or stars present), omitted otherwise. `productivity_index`\nv2 (same file; current index fields at lines 1046-1049): **per-query suggestion adoption** =\n(distinct hh_events queries with â‰¥1 `loaded`) / (distinct queries surfaced), 7-day window\nauto-widening to all-time until â‰¥10 queries (fallback labeled in a `window` field); JSON carries\n`window`, `sample_size`; `no_data` only at zero queries ever. `finds_new` excludes papers via the\nsame kind-agnostic URL/slug patterns. `briefing_delivery.build_session_note` (lines 80-96) renders\nthe new top-find lines (name + why + quality-when-present) and the \"suggestion adoption\" wording.\nAdditive updates to `tests/test_wave1_visibility.py` (the session-note tests at lines 131-205) +\nnew fixture tests for the eligibility gate and the adoption formula.\n\n**Depends on:** â€”\n\n**done-when:** Verifiable ON DEMAND (run `morning_briefing.py` against the live KB and inspect the\nemitted session_note/`latest_summary.json` â€” the 06:47 deadline is a deploy deadline, not the\nacceptance gate): the session_note contains zero raw IDs and zero `local:`/vendor/paper entries;\nevery top find is a named eligible artifact with a why-line; the productivity line reads\n\"suggestion adoption\" with window + sample size; one clean commit; `python -m pytest` green with\nadditive-only test changes.\n\n- **Given** today's real KB (mis-kinded arxiv rows included), **when** the briefing runs, **then** top_finds contains only eligible non-paper/non-model/non-local artifacts with `name/kind/why` fields and the session_note renders them as named lines.\n- **Given** a FIXTURE hh_events set of 20 distinct queries of which 5 have â‰¥1 `loaded`, **when** the index computes, **then** it reports 25% adoption, window=all-time (labeled fallback because the 7-day window has <10 queries), sample_size=20 â€” never a bare 0% from a thin window; a separate live sanity check asserts adoption âˆˆ [0,1] and a labeled window. [SUBTLE â€” the 0%-with-status-ok trap]\n- **Given** an artifact with `local:` canonical_url or a vendor-denylist domain, **then** it can never appear in top_finds (regression-tested).\n- **Given** zero hh_events queries ever (fixture), **then** status is `no_data` (and only then).\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Right kind at ingest + catalog backfills + serving-surface trust\n\n**Intent:** Stop noise at the source and make the existing catalog trustworthy: arxivâ†’paper at\nscreen time, vendor/blog rejection with a registry allowlist, the awesome-list fix at its real root\ncause (the discovery-queue DRAIN path, E21 â€” the scout-level fix already exists), audited backfills\nthat own the library