N_INTEREST` (default 0.3) AND older than\n`AURORA_RETIRE_AGE_DAYS` (default 60) â†’ retire (env-overridable defaults; the defaults are the\ndecision); **acceptance is fixture-based** (live stale-retirements need ~2 weeks of probe history\nby design; the live leg is armed, not demonstrated). Digest value section: suggestion-adoption\ntrend, loads/dismissals this week, profile-drift hints (most-dismissed kinds/domains vs profile\nemphases â†’ prompts a manual `INTEREST_PROFILE.md` edit; NO auto-mutation).\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 4\n\n**done-when:** Fixture hh_events demonstrably shift both HH match ranking and top-finds order (tests\nprove boost + decay + the Â±0.10 bound); the retirement policy runs nightly unattended with\nfixture-proven rules and the live leg armed (N=2, threshold/age defaults set); the digest shows the\nvalue section; plugin rebuilt + handed to John for reinstall + smoked after reinstall; clean\ncommitted tree; `python -m pytest` green.\n\n- **Given** an artifact with loaded history, **then** its match score rises by at most 0.10; **given** dismissed history, it falls by at most 0.10; **given** 30-day-old events, the effect is halved. [SUBTLE â€” unbounded feedback trap]\n- **Given** a fixture artifact with 2 consecutive stale probes, **then** the policy retires it (audited); **given** only 1, it does not.\n- **Given** a week of usage, **then** the digest's value section reports adoption trend + loads/dismissals and surfaces drift hints without modifying the profile.\n","numLines":223,"startLine":1,"totalLines":223}}}
