or badged, never `local:`) artifact with a one-line why and a quality signal when discriminating.\n26\t- A standing noise audit returns 0 (no arxiv-as-tool/agent, no vendor-blog tools, no pointer\n27\t  artifacts, no dead library links, no retired rows in serving surfaces).\n28\t- Every new find carries `interest_score` + `interest_why`, scored against `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`,\n29\t  metered at a non-zero priced rate, capped nightly.\n30\t- `productivity_index` = per-query suggestion adoption from `hh_events` (window labeled, sample size\n31\t  shown); usage (loaded/dismissed) demonstrably shifts ranking via a bounded modifier.\n32\t- The weekly digest ships on schedule with ranked finds, the papers stream, and catalog-health deltas.\n33\t- Locked-preserved intact: KB schema (additive migrations only) + browsable library, single-owner\n34\t  security gate, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand MCP + publisher.\n35\t\n36\t## Hard constraints\n37\t- Evolve, don't rebuild (researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict). No discovery-engine parallelism. Issue #5\n38\t  (H1 fetch reliability) is out of scope.\n39\t- Backfills re-kind/retire ONLY â€” never DELETE rows; `--dry-run` + `--audit-out` mandatory on every\n40\t  backfill; `bin/migrate_to_kind_paper.py`'s delete step must never run again (it would delete 3\n41\t  legitimate local skills, ids 822-824).\n42\t- Library is a filesystem surface: any re-kind/retire owns the page moves + `regenerate_indexes`;\n43\t  the publisher must never ship retired pages (predicate must evaluate BEFORE the\n44\t  `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` early-return at `publisher.py:78-79`).\n45\t- Scheduled tasks execute `C:\\dev\\aurora` directly (the working tree IS production; sweeps at\n46\t  01:07/02:19/03:41/05:03, briefing 06:47): every wave ends with a clean committed tree.\n47\t- Any wave touching `helping-hand-plugin/mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py` ends with plugin rebuild\n48\t  (`bin/build-plugin.py`) + reinstall + live smoke â€” the runtime is the installed plugin, not the repo.\n49\t- test-command: `python -m pytest`. 915-test baseline stays green; no test weakening; the count may\n50\t  only rise.\n51\t\n52\t## Provenance\n53\tMaster plan (Crucible Stage 1, two Shark-Tank rounds + independent Judge, user-approved 2026-06-09):\n54\t`docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md` â€” evidence base E1â€“E23 all code/DB-grounded. Stage-2\n55\tverification (HH scorer seam, stars budget, dupe set, source-gate false positives, drain-path seam)\n56\tcompleted 2026-06-09 and folded into the waves below.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cce77bb-c3d3-45f2-bc43-fe5326cf011c","uuid":"c66a452a-8a76-46c7-8b9a-1e8560484684","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:51:36.355Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-quality\\DESCRIPTION.md","content":"# Aurora Discovery Quality & Surfacing (\"water quality\") â€” Description\n\n**North Star (locked 2026-06-09):** Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified,\ngenuinely interesting, and worth his attention â€” a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed,\nmeasurable value loop â€” built by evolving the existing pipeline, never touching the proven plumbing.\nPhase 1+2 plumbing (security hardening, cost telemetry, briefing delivery, llm.py upgrades) is done\nand green; this phase is ONLY about what flows through the pipe: classification at ingest, catalog\nhygiene, taste-ranked surfacing, and the usage value loop.\n\nSix locked criteria (each wave serves â‰¥1): (1) right kind at ingest â€” arxiv never lands as\ntool/agent again, vendor posts and pointer rows never become tools, OpenRouter is a reference table;\n(2) top finds are named, ranked, eligible artifacts with a why-line â€” never raw IDs; (3) a persisted\ninterest (taste) score drives ranking; (4) productivity derives from real `hh_events` usage and\nusage feeds back into ranking; (5) the catalog is trustworthy â€” noise backfilled, dupes merged,\nst