{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01G8tcviqM9sAk4uoH76qJHe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# foreman-handoff-quality â€” Grounded Bullet Claims\n\n**Source:** `docs/foreman-handoff-quality/{DESCRIPTION.md, IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md}` â€” the Foreman-ready handoff for the Aurora Discovery Quality & Surfacing (\"water quality\") phase. Master plan + evidence (E1â€“E23) in `docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md`, Crucible Stage-1 approved 2026-06-09 (two Shark-Tank rounds + independent Judge).\n\n## Scope & North Star\n- **North Star (locked 2026-06-09):** everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting, and worth his attention â€” a *smaller, high-trust catalog* with a *closed, measurable value loop*, built by **evolving the existing pipeline**, never rebuilding (researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict).\n- This phase touches only *what flows through the pipe* (classification, hygiene, taste-ranked surfacing, usage loop); Phase 1+2 plumbing (security gate, cost telemetry, briefing delivery, llm.py) is done/green and locked-preserved.\n- **OUT of scope:** discovery-engine parallelism; issue #5 (H1 fetch reliability).\n\n## Hard constraints (carried into every wave)\n- **Backfills re-kind/retire ONLY â€” never DELETE.** `--dry-run` + `--audit-out` mandatory; working sets resolved by RULE in the dry-run pass, never by the drift-prone 2026-06-09 snapshot counts.\n- `bin/migrate_to_kind_paper.py`'s **delete step must never run again** â€” it would delete 3 legitimate local skills (ids 822â€“824).\n- The **working tree IS production** (sweeps 01:07/02:19/03:41/05:03, briefing 06:47); every wave ends with a **clean committed tree**.\n- Library is a filesystem surface: any re-kind/retire owns the page moves + `regenerate_indexes`.\n- Publisher `retired_at` predicate must evaluate **BEFORE** the `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` early-return at `publisher.py:78-79` (E20 dead-code-placement trap).\n- Any `server.py` (aurora-kb) change ends with plugin rebuild + **MANUAL reinstall by John** + live smoke â€” runtime is the installed plugin, not the repo.\n- KB schema = additive migrations only; **915-test baseline stays green, no weakening, count may only rise** (`python -m pytest`).\n\n## The five waves (run in series)\n- **Wave 1 â€” De-noised ranked top finds + honest adoption metric.** Briefing-side only (`morning_briefing.py`, `briefing_delivery.py`); no DB/pipeline change, so correct even while tonight's rows stay mis-kinded. Replaces `id DESC LIMIT 5` with an eligibility gate (GitHub/badge, excludes `local:`, models, papers, vendor denylist, pointer rows); ranked find emits `name/kind/why/quality`; `productivity_index` v2 = per-query suggestion adoption with labeled window + sample_size (avoids the 0%-from-thin-window trap). Deploy deadline 06:47, but acceptance is on-demand.\n- **Wave 2 â€” Right kind at ingest + catalog backfills + serving-surface trust.** arxivâ†’paper at screen time; source-type gate rejecting vendor/blog/aggregator URLs **with a package-registry allowlist** (pypi/npm/crates.io/â€¦ â€” false-positive trap); awesome-list fix at its real root (the discovery-queue DRAIN seam, E21, `orchestrator.py:663`); audited re-kind/retire backfills (arxiv ~96, nvidia ~50, pointer ~31-34, dedupe 8 version pairs) that own library dir-moves; publisher retired_at predicate; HH D1 (models excluded from single-mode routing/telemetry, kept in ranked/compare) + D2 (papers stay matchable in pull, labeled, never auto-loaded); `bin/noise_audit.py` standing zero-noise check.\n- **Wave 3 â€” Weekly digest v1 + notability signal.** Schedules the already-built `check_link_health.py` (stars/staleness); one supervised backfill over ~283 GitHub-linked artifacts (**PRECONDITION: authenticated gh CLI â€” HALT-AND-ASK if not**); `bin/weekly_digest.py` â†’ `reports/weekly/<date>.md` with ranked finds, a \"papers worth reading\" stream, and catalog-health deltas. done-when â‰¥80% active GitHub artifacts have stargazers.\n- **Wave 4 â€” The taste score.** Persisted interestingness score tuned to `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md` (John-editable); migration `0025_interest_score.sql` (additive: `interest_score`, `interest_why`, `interest_scored_at`); `roles/taste.py` priced + metered through CostRecorder (E17 unpriced-tag trap â€” priced key must equal called tag), nightly cap (default 40) with heuristic fallback; ranking switches to `interest_score`. Scope = new finds + any unscored artifact reaching a serving surface, never the back catalog. Nightly leg armed, not demonstrated in-build.\n- **Wave 5 â€” Close the loop.** Bounded usage modifier in HH `_compute_matches` (**Â±0.10 on cosine, 30-day half-life** â€” decided) applied to matches + top_finds + digest; `bin/retirement_policy.py` (N=2 consecutive stale probes â†’ retire; never-surfaced + low-interest + aged â†’ retire; env-overridable defaults, reversible, fixture-based acceptance); digest value section (adoption trend, loads/dismissals, profile-drift hints, **no auto-mutation**).\n\n## Locked user-gate decisions\n- Papers = opt-in stream (`kind='paper'`, never pushed, in weekly digest, matchable+labeled in HH pull â€” D2).\n- Vendor blog posts rejected at ingest.\n- Taste scorer approved at cents/night (metered, capped).\n- HH model rows excluded from single-mode routing + surfaced-telemetry but recallable in ranked/compare (D1).\n\n---\n\nThese are grounded in the two handoff documents as written. Want me to write this to memory (the index already has a [Discovery quality plan] entry I could update), or check `EXECUTION-LOG.md` to report which waves Foreman has actually completed so far?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9934,"cache_read_input_tokens":32961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9934},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cce77bb-c3d3-45f2-bc43-fe5326cf011c","uuid":"95b1f3d6-f665-4bad-bb38-005514191815","request_id":"req_011CcKGvnEaQbGagSCNUnHc1"}
